# AWS Management Console Getting Started Guide

> Provides a short introduction to working with the AWS Management Console, including tips on getting information about your account and about billing.

- [Using the AWS Management Console with our new AWS experience](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/simplified-console.md)
- [Getting started with a service](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/start-service.md)
- [AWS managed policies](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/security-iam-awsmanpol.md)
- [Markdown in AWS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/aws-markdown.md)
- [Troubleshooting](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/troubleshooting.md)
- [Document history](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/document-history.md)

## [What is the AWS Management Console?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/what-is.md)

- [Individual AWS service consoles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/individual-console.md): Each AWS service has its own individual service console that you can access within the AWS Management Console.
- [Accessing the AWS Management Console with mobile devices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/console-device.md): The AWS Management Console is designed to work on tablets as well as other kinds of mobile devices:


## [Unified Navigation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/unified-navigation.md)

- [Accessing the Services menu](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/service-menu.md): You can access the Services menu (represented by a grid ⋮⋮⋮) to view a list of AWS services, as well as your recently visited services and services you added to your Favorites list..

### [Searching for products, services, features, and more](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/using-search.md)

The search box in the navigation bar provides a unified search tool for finding AWS services and features, service documentation, and AWS Marketplace.

- [Searching for AWS products](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/unified-search-regular.md): The following procedure details how to search for AWS products using the search tool.
- [Refining your search](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/unified-search-refine.md): You can refine your search by content type and view additional information about search results.
- [Viewing features of a service](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/unified-search-top-result.md): You can view features of a service from within your search results.
- [Launching AWS CloudShell](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/launch-cloudshell.md): AWS CloudShell is a browser-based, pre-authenticated shell that you can launch directly from the AWS Management Console on the navigation bar.
- [Accessing AWS notifications and Health events](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/access-notifications.md): Accessing event information.
- [Getting support](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/getting-support.md): This topic includes information about getting support in the AWS Management Console.

### [Configuring the AWS Management Console](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/working-with-console.md)

This topic describes how to configure your AWS Management Console using the Unified Settings page to set defaults that apply to all service consoles.

### [Configuring Unified Settings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/unified-settings.md)

Configure settings that will apply to all service consoles in the AWS Management Console.

- [Accessing Unified Settings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/access-unified-settings.md): How to access AWS Management Console.
- [Resetting Unified Settings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/reset-unified-settings.md): Rest your console settings in AWS Management Console.
- [Editing Unified Settings](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/edit-unified-settings.md): Configure settings that will apply to all service consoles in the AWS Management Console.
- [Changing your visual mode](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/visual-mode-unified-settings.md): Configure settings that will apply to all service consoles in the AWS Management Console.

### [Configuring visible Regions and services](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/visible-regions-services.md)

Configure which AWS Regions and AWS services are visible in the AWS Management Console navigation for your account.

- [Prerequisites](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/visible-regions-services-prereqs.md): Required IAM permissions for configuring visible Regions and services in the AWS Management Console.
- [Configuring visible Regions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/configure-visible-regions.md): Configure which AWS Regions are visible in the AWS Management Console Region selector for your account.
- [Configuring visible services](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/configure-visible-services.md): Configure which AWS services are visible in the AWS Management Console Services menu for your account.
- [Enabling experimental preview](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/experimental-preview.md): Opt in to AWS experimental preview to access new features that are still being evaluated in the AWS Management Console.

### [Choosing your Region](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/select-region.md)

For many services, you can choose an AWS Region that specifies where your resources are managed.

- [Choosing a Region from the navigation bar](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/select-region-procedure.md): For many services, you can choose an AWS Region that specifies where your resources are managed.
- [Setting default Region](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/change-default-region.md): For many services, you can choose an AWS Region that specifies where your resources are managed.

### [Favorites](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/add-remove-shortcut.md)

Learn how to access your frequently used services more quickly, by saving their service consoles to a list of Favorites.

### [Adding favorites](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/add-fave.md)

You can add services and applications to your favorites from the Services menu and the Recently visited menu.

- [Adding services](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/add-fave-services.md): You can add services to your favorites from the Services menu or the search results page from the search box.
- [Adding apps](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/add-fave-apps.md): You can add applications to your favorites from the Services menu.
- [Accessing favorites](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/access-fave.md): You can access services and applications added to your favorites from the Services menu, the favorites quickbar, and the Favorites widget.
- [Removing favorites](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/remove-fave.md): You can remove services and applications from your favorites using the Services menu.

### [Changing your password](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/change-password.md)

If you are an account owner, you can change your AWS account password from the AWS Management Console.

- [Root users](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/root-password.md): If you are a Root user, you can change your AWS account password from the AWS Management Console.
- [IAM users](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/iam-password.md): If you are an IAM user, you can change your AWS account password from the AWS Management Console or an AWS access portal.
- [IAM Identity Center users](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/idc-password.md): If you are an AWS IAM Identity Center user, you can change your AWS account password from an AWS access portal.
- [Federated identities](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/fed-password.md): If you use a federated identity, you can change your AWS account password from an AWS access portal.
- [Changing the language of the AWS Management Console](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/change-language.md): Learn how to change the language for the AWS Management Console.

### [Accessing your AWS information](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/acctinfo.md)

You can access information about your AWS account from the console and get information about billing, organizations, and more.

- [Accessing account information](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/ainfo.md): If you have the necessary permissions, you can access information about your AWS charges from the console.
- [Accessing organization information](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/organizationsinfo.md): If you have the necessary permissions, you can access information about your AWS organizations.
- [Accessing service quota information](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/quotasinfo.md): If you have the necessary permissions, you can access information about your AWS service quotas.
- [Accessing billing information](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/billinginfo.md): If you have the necessary permissions, you can access information about your AWS charges from the console.
- [Signing in to multiple accounts](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/multisession.md): This topic includes information about how to sign in to multiple accounts.

### [Using recommended actions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/recommended-actions.md)

Learn about recommended actions in the AWS Management Console that help you complete tasks and implement best practices.

- [Monitoring with CloudTrail logs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/log-using-cloudtrail-rec-actions.md): Learn about logging AWS Recommended Actions with AWS CloudTrail.


## [AWS Console Home](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/customizing-ch.md)

- [Viewing all AWS services](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/view-services.md): You can view a list of all AWS services and access their consoles from Console Home.
- [Working with Widgets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/work-with-widgets.md): The Console Home dashboard includes widgets that display important information about your AWS environment and provide shortcuts to your services.

### [myApplications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/aws-myApplications.md)

This topic describes how to configure and use myApplications on AWS.

- [myApplications availability change](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/aws-myApplications-availability-change.md): Information about changes to myApplications availability.
- [Supported Regions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/supported-regions.md): myApplications is available in the following AWS Regions:

### [Applications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/myApp-manage-apps.md)

This topic covers how to manage your applications. myApplications uses AppRegistry to manage applications.

- [Creating applications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/myApp-getting-started.md): get started with myApplications.
- [Onboarding applications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/myApp-step1-onboard-existing.md): This procedure details how to onboard an existing application.
- [Viewing applications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/myApp-step2.md): View applications
- [Editing applications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/myApp-edit-app.md): Editing your application opens AppRegistry so you can update its description.
- [Deleting applications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/myApp-delete-app.md): You can delete applications if they are no longer needed.
- [Creating code snippets](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/myApp-gne-code.md): myApplications creates code snippets for all of your applications.

### [Resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/myApp-manage-resources.md)

This topic covers how to manage your resources.

### [Adding resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/myApp-add-resources.md)

Adding resources to your applications allows you to group them and manage their security, performance, and compliance.

- [Resolving tag-sync errors in myApplications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/sync-error.md): This section describes common tag-sync errors and how to resolve them.
- [Removing resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/myApp-remove-resources.md): You can remove resources to disassociate them from your application.
- [Viewing resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/viewing-resources.md): You can view your application resources from myApplications and the Services menu.
- [myApplications dashboard](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/myApp-app-dash.md): Access application details from the application dashboard.
- [Chatting with Amazon Q](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/ask-q.md): Ask Amazon Q questions about AWS.


## [AWS Management Console Private Access](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/console-private-access.md)

- [Supported AWS Regions, service consoles, and features](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/supported-regions-consoles.md): Learn about AWS Regions, services, and features supported by AWS Management Console Private Access.
- [Configuring VPC endpoints](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/required-endpoints-dns-configuration.md): Learn about the required VPC endpoints for AWS Management Console Private Access.
- [Configuring DNS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/dns-configuration-console-signin.md): Learn about the required DNS configuration for AWS Management Console Private Access.

### [Implementing access controls](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/implementing-access-controls.md)

Learn about how to implement access controls for AWS Management Console Private Access.

- [Trusted identities](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/trusted-identities.md): Restrict which AWS accounts and organizational identities can sign in through your AWS Management Console Private Access endpoints.
- [Trusted resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/trusted-resources.md): Restrict which resources users can access through the AWS Management Console to those that belong to your AWS organization.
- [Expected networks](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/expected-networks.md): Enforce that users access the AWS Management Console only from approved networks, such as your VPCs or on-premises data centers.

### [Getting started with a test environment](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/try-out-private-access.md)

Learn about how to set up and test AWS Management Console Private Access in a new account.

- [Test setup with Amazon EC2](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/test-console-private-access-EC2.md): Learn about how to test setup and experience an AWS Management Console Private Access connection to Amazon Simple Storage Service from an Amazon EC2 instance.
- [Test setup with Amazon WorkSpaces](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/test-console-private-access-workspaces.md): Learn about how to test setup with Amazon WorkSpaces.
- [Reference architecture](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/console-private-access-reference-architectures.md): Learn about architecture set up for connecting AWS Site-to-Site VPN to AWS Virtual Private Gateway (VGW).


## [AWS User Experience Customization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/uxc.md)

- [Getting started](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/getting-started-uxc.md): Learn how to configure account color, service visibility, and Region visibility for the AWS Management Console.
- [API Reference](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/uxc-api-reference.md): Reference documentation for the AWS User Experience Customization API.
- [Monitoring with CloudTrail logs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/log-using-cloudtrail.md): Learn about logging AWS User Experience Customization with AWS CloudTrail.

### [Security](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/security.md)

Configure AWS User Experience Customization to meet your security and compliance objectives, and learn how to use other AWS services that help you to secure your UXC resources.

### [Identity and Access Management](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/security_iam.md)

Learn how AWS Identity and Access Management controls access to AWS User Experience Customization resources.

- [How User Experience Customization works with IAM](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/security_iam_service-with-iam.md): AWS User Experience Customization (UXC) works with IAM policies to manage access to UXC API Operations.
- [Identity-based policy examples](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awsconsolehelpdocs/latest/gsg/security_iam_id-based-policy-examples.md): By default, users and roles don't have permission to get or modify UXC resources.


